# Web Deployment Plan

## Goal Description
Deploy the Flutter web application to a web hosting service. Given the project's existing usage of Firebase (Functions, Firestore), Firebase Hosting is the recommended and assumed target.

## User Review Required
- **Hosting Service**: Assuming Firebase Hosting based on project history.
- **Build Configuration**: Will use `flutter build web --release`.

## Proposed Changes
### Configuration
- **[MODIFY]** [firebase.json](file:///d:/nexonn/go_buddy_app/go_buddy/firebase.json)
    - Add `"hosting"` key pointing to `"public": "build/web"`.
    - Add rewrites for Single Page App (SPA) behavior: `"source": "**", "destination": "/index.html"`.
- **[NEW]** `.firebaserc`
    - Set default project to `payservices-7827a`.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- Run `flutter build web` to ensure the project builds successfully.

### Manual Verification
- After deployment, visit the provided Hosting URL to verify the app loads correctly.
